Wafer Inspection Helps Improve SiC Manufacturing Yields

SiC production involves defects that can originate during crystal growth, wafering, polishing or epitaxial processing. Inspection systems help detect particles, scratches, pits and crystallographic defects before additional processing increases the cost of defective material.

Metrology systems measure wafer geometry, surface characteristics and layer uniformity.

The Transition to Larger Wafers Increases Inspection Requirements

The transition from 150 mm to 200 mm SiC manufacturing is a major structural driver. Larger wafers can increase potential die output, but they also raise the value exposed to wafer-level defects and process variation.

Automated inspection and reliable measurement data can help manufacturers strengthen process control.

